# 🔟 Work and Days

For the same efficiency:

$$
\boxed{
Workers\times Days=Constant
}
$$

Example:

10 workers finish a job in 12 days.

How many days for 15 workers?

$$
10\times12=15\times x
$$

$$
120=15x
$$

$$
\boxed{x=8}
$$

---

# 1️⃣1️⃣ Workers × Days × Hours

If working hours also change:

$$
\boxed{
Workers\times Days\times Hours
=Constant
}
$$

assuming the workers have the same efficiency.

Example:

10 workers work 8 hours/day for 12 days.

If 16 workers work 6 hours/day, how many days?

$$
10\times8\times12
=
16\times6\times x
$$

$$
960=96x
$$

$$
\boxed{x=10\ days}
$$

---

# 1️⃣2️⃣ Three People Working Together

Suppose:

A → 10 days
B → 15 days
C → 30 days

Take:

$$
LCM=30
$$

Efficiencies:

```text
A → 3
B → 2
C → 1
```

Combined:

$$
3+2+1=6
$$

Time:

$$
30/6
$$

$$
\boxed5\text{ days}
$$

---

# 🔥 1️⃣3️⃣ One Person Leaves

A, B and C together finish a job in 6 days.

Suppose their rates are:

$$
A=2,\ B=3,\ C=1
$$

Total:

$$
6
$$

If C leaves:

$$
2+3=5
$$

Total work = 36 units if using 6 days × 6 units/day.

New time:

$$
36/5
$$

$$
\boxed7.2\text{ days}
$$

---

# 1️⃣4️⃣ Alternate Working

Suppose:

A can complete work in 6 days.

B can complete work in 12 days.

Take total work:

$$
LCM(6,12)=12
$$

A:

$$
12/6=2\ units/day
$$

B:

$$
12/12=1\ unit/day
$$

If they work alternately starting with A:

```text
Day 1 → A = 2
Day 2 → B = 1
Day 3 → A = 2
Day 4 → B = 1
...
```

Every 2 days:

$$
3\ units
$$

Total work:

$$
12
$$

After 8 days:

$$
4\times3=12
$$

So:

$$
\boxed8\text{ days}
$$

---

# 1️⃣5️⃣ Pipes & Cisterns 🚰

Pipes are simply **Time & Work questions**.

The difference:

* Filling pipe → **positive work**
* Emptying pipe → **negative work**

---

# 1️⃣6️⃣ Filling Pipe

A pipe fills a tank in 10 hours.

Rate:

$$
\boxed{\frac1{10}}
$$

of the tank per hour.

Another fills it in 20 hours:

$$
\boxed{\frac1{20}}
$$

Together:

$$
\frac1{10}+\frac1{20}
$$

$$
=\frac3{20}
$$

Time:

$$
\frac{20}{3}
$$

$$
\boxed{6.67\ hours}
$$

---

# 1️⃣7️⃣ Filling + Emptying

A pipe fills a tank in 6 hours.

An outlet empties it in 12 hours.

Fill rate:

$$
\frac16
$$

Empty rate:

$$
-\frac1{12}
$$

Net rate:

$$
\frac16-\frac1{12}
$$

$$
=\frac1{12}
$$

Therefore:

$$
\boxed{12\ hours}
$$

---

# 🔥 1️⃣8️⃣ Important Rule

```text
Filling pipe → +

Emptying pipe → -
```

Never add an emptying pipe's rate.

---

# 1️⃣9️⃣ Three Pipes

A fills in 10 hours.

B fills in 20 hours.

C empties in 40 hours.

Net rate:

$$
\frac1{10}+\frac1{20}-\frac1{40}
$$

LCM = 40:

$$
\frac4{40}+\frac2{40}-\frac1{40}
$$

$$
=\frac5{40}
$$

$$
=\frac18
$$

Therefore:

$$
\boxed8\ hours}
$$

---

# 🧠 2️⃣0️⃣ Leak Problem

A tank can be filled by a pipe in 5 hours.

A leak can empty the tank in 20 hours.

Pipe rate:

$$
\frac15
$$

Leak rate:

$$
-\frac1{20}
$$

Net:

$$
\frac15-\frac1{20}
$$

$$
=\frac4{20}-\frac1{20}
$$

$$
=\frac3{20}
$$

Time:

$$
\frac{20}{3}
$$

$$
\boxed6.67\ hours}
$$

---

# 2️⃣1️⃣ Work Done in a Given Time

A completes work in 8 days.

How much work does A do in 3 days?

Daily rate:

$$
1/8
$$

Therefore:

$$
3\times\frac18
$$

$$
\boxed{\frac38}
$$

So A completes **37.5%** of the work.

---

# 2️⃣2️⃣ Remaining Work

If A completes:

$$
\frac38
$$

then remaining:

$$
1-\frac38
$$

$$
=\boxed{\frac58}
$$

---

# 🔥 2️⃣3️⃣ A Very Important Pattern

If A takes:

$$
10\text{ days}
$$

then:

```text
1 day → 1/10
2 days → 2/10
3 days → 3/10
...
```

If working at constant efficiency:

$$
\boxed{Work\propto Time}
$$

---

# 2️⃣4️⃣ Men and Women Problems

Suppose:

2 men do the same work as 3 women.

Then:

$$
2M=3W
$$

Therefore:

$$
M:W=3:2
$$

So:

> 1 man = 1.5 women in efficiency.

These questions are solved by converting everyone into a **common efficiency unit**.

---

# 2️⃣5️⃣ Example

4 men can finish a job in 12 days.

How long will 6 men take?

$$
4\times12=6x
$$

$$
48=6x
$$

$$
\boxed8\ days
$$

---

# 2️⃣6️⃣ Men + Women

Suppose:

1 man = 2 women.

Then:

4 men + 6 women

Convert men:

$$
4M=8W
$$

Therefore total:

$$
8W+6W
$$

$$
=14W
$$

Now the problem becomes a normal work-rate problem.

---

# 🧮 2️⃣7️⃣ GATE/Placement Example

A can finish a job in 12 days and B in 18 days.

How long together?

Using shortcut:

$$
\frac{12\times18}{12+18}
$$

$$
=\frac{216}{30}
$$

$$
\boxed7.2\ days}
$$

---

# 🧮 2️⃣8️⃣ Another

A and B together complete work in 8 days.

A alone completes it in 12 days.

Find B's time.

Combined rate:

$$
\frac18
$$

A's rate:

$$
\frac1{12}
$$

B's rate:

$$
\frac18-\frac1{12}
$$

LCM 24:

$$
\frac3{24}-\frac2{24}
$$

$$
=\frac1{24}
$$

Therefore:

$$
\boxed{24\ days}
$$

---

# 🧮 2️⃣9️⃣ Pipe Example

Pipe A fills a tank in 8 hours.

Pipe B fills it in 12 hours.

Together:

$$
\frac18+\frac1{12}
$$

LCM = 24:

$$
\frac3{24}+\frac2{24}
$$

$$
=\frac5{24}
$$

Time:

$$
\boxed{\frac{24}{5}=4.8\ hours}
$$

